<title>USA: Sun says pact calls for 175 hourly jobs to go.</title>
<headline>Sun says pact calls for 175 hourly jobs to go.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sun Co Inc and the Oil, Chemical and Atomic Workers (OCAW) union reached a tentative agreement to cut 175 hourly positions at the Sun's troubled Marcus Hook, Pennsylvania refinery, the company said.</p>
<p>Sun and the union spent the past month in negotiations regarding the cutbacks, which had originally targeted 235 positions at the refinery.</p>
<p>The union had threatened to break the contract and go on strike over the cutbacks at the refinery, which has an estimated capacity of 175,000 barrels per day.</p>
